<br />
At this time, the Red Cross is not proactively asking for blood donations as part of our Red Cross disaster response in Texas, but the need for blood is constant. The Red Cross currently has an urgent need for blood and platelet donations across the country due to a summer decline in blood donors and blood drive sponsors. In Texas, we are closely monitoring our blood supplies amid this ongoing disaster. With dangerous widespread flooding in Southeast Texas, all blood collection organizations in the U.S. are making efforts to meet patient blood needs and to ensure a sufficient blood supply in storm affected areas. Blood donations are always encouraged and the Red Cross stands ready to provide blood products as needed.<br />
<br />
One way to help is to consider supporting a local blood drive in your area to help raise awareness for blood donations. &nbsp;You can find blood drives near you at www.redcrossblood.org.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Another way to help is to donate financially to the Red Cross to help people affected by Hurricane Harvey. &nbsp;Visit www.redcross.org, call 1-800-RED CROSS, or by texting the word HARVEY to 90999 to make a $10 donation. &nbsp;<br />
&nbsp;<br />
Thanks so much for considering the American Red Cross. &nbsp;Please contact me with any questions you may have!&nbsp;<br />
